Amiga (Minimig) core: vendored from NanoMig.

The partial bitstream of this core is published as a `.cor` together with this source. No Kickstart, Workbench or other
ROM is in this repository or in any package.
Rights holders who see a problem with any part listed here: please contact us, and we remove the part concerned.

Upstream: https://github.com/MiSTle-Dev/NanoMig, commit a19604a19a6100033a29281d2be3287b65bc9c0e (2026-10-11).
The repository has no LICENSE file. The files' own headers decide; they are kept as they came.

  src/minimig-aga/*.v   Minimig-AGA chipset (Dennis van Weeren, Jakub Bednarski, Rok Krajnc, Alexey Melnikov, Tobias
                        Gubener and others). Most headers: GPL v3 or later. About 40 files carry no licence text;
                        ide.v is BSD-3-clause (Alexey Melnikov). cpu_cache_new.v and denise_colortable_ram_mf.v are not
                        taken. Changes of ours are marked "TRX" in the files.
  src/fx68k/*           FX68K 68000 core, Jorge Cwik; directory LICENSE: GPL v3.
  src/nanomig.v         Wrapper of NanoMig (Till Harbaum et al.), no licence text in the header.

Not taken: TG68K, the Tang tops, Gowin IP, HDMI, MCU/SD/OSD glue, SDRAM controller (all replaced by host services and
cores/amiga/rtl/trx). Kickstart and Workbench are not in this repository.
